	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">-</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">When a Pokémon learns Flash, you can\nilluminate caves no matter how dark\fthey may be.\rYou can try it on BELLSPROUT,\nfor example...</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">I hope you learn and grow from\nyour journey.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">It’s a powerful painting of a\nBELLSPROUT.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A Pokémon statue...\nIt looks very distinguished.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ELDER LI: Ah. The one battling\ntheir way up while the other two\frearrange my tower like it is a\ndollhouse.\rThe tower bends. It does not\npanic.\rToday it panicked--and I find I am\nless angry at the boy than at how\fEASILY it was done.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ELDER LI: I will not reopen these\ndoors for an apology. Apologies\fare cheap, and the boy’s would be\ncounterfeit anyway.\rI reopen them because of HOW YOU\nCLIMBED.\rYou fought my sages with patience.\nYou respected what this place\fteaches. That is the apology that\ncounts.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ELDER LI: Take this. The tower’s\nold light, for the dark places the\fyoung insist on entering.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ELDER LI: Now go. The next time\nyou climb my tower, do it with\fsteadier hands.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">ELDER LI: The tags the boy\nscattered still flutter where they\fdo not belong.\rReturn what was misplaced.\nThen we will speak.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A paper training tag is tucked\nunder the incense bowl, doing its\fbest to look ceremonial.\rIt is very much not supposed to be\nhere.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0056_D15R0103_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">{STRVAR_1 3, 0, 0} rescued the training\ntag from under the bowl!\rOne of Ren’s--the type symbols give\nit away.</language>
	</row>
</body>
